---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import HeroSection from "../../components/HeroSection.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | NUS Seafarers"
  description="Learn about our mission and crew."
>
  <HeroSection
    title="Anchored in heritage, sailing toward a sustainable future."
    subtitle="Born from voyages aboard Four Friends, we unite people through adventure, community, and care for the sea — keeping maritime traditions alive while charting a course for a greener tomorrow."
    path="about"
  />

  <section class="w-full px-6 sm:px-12 md:px-32 pb-24">
    <div
      class="grid lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start max-w-5xl mx-auto pb-16"
    >
      <!-- Left rail -->
      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <div class="text-xl lg:text-2xl text-neutral-500">Our Story</div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Right content -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <h2
          class="text-3xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl leading-tight font-medium text-neutral-700"
        >
          NUS Seafarers began with sailing voyages aboard Four Friends, a 60
          foot gaff-rigged schooner. These early trips were about bringing
          experiential sailing voyages to students.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="grid lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start max-w-5xl mx-auto"
    >
      <!-- Left rail -->
      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-6"></aside>

      <!-- Right content -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <img
          src="/images/about/our_story_1.jpg"
          alt="North with the Trade Winds"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full object-cover"
        />

        <!-- Optional supporting copy -->
        <h2
          class="text-neutral-900 font-semibold text-md max-w-3xl leading-tight"
        >
          Driven by the spirit of adventure, exploring the unique cultural and
          economic heritage of maritime Southeast Asia and complex ecology of
          Singapore waters.
        </h2>

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          NUS Seafarers became an official student club in 2025, fully
          student-run. We realised that sailing could be more than just
          adventure; it could be a platform for sustainability, community, and
          heritage. Today, it is a platform to bring together people from all
          backgrounds to learn to sail, join coastal cleanups, share maritime
          stories, and connect with the ocean in meaningful ways.
        </p>

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          From our first days on Four Friends to our diverse activities now, our
          aim has stayed the same: to enjoy the sea, care for it, and keep its
          stories alive.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="w-full px-6 sm:px-12 md:px-32 pb-24">
    <div
      class="grid lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start max-w-5xl mx-auto pb-16"
    >
      <!-- Left rail -->
      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <div class="text-xl lg:text-2xl text-neutral-500">Our Mission</div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Right content -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <h2
          class="text-3xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl leading-tight font-medium text-neutral-700"
        >
          NUS Seafarers began with a simple idea: that the sea should be for
          everyone - open, welcoming, and cared for.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="grid lg:grid-cols-[220px_1fr] gap-10 lg:gap-16 items-start max-w-5xl mx-auto"
    >
      <!-- Left rail -->
      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-6"></aside>

      <!-- Right content -->
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <img
          src="/images/sailing/weekend_race_series_1_2025/racing_boat.png"
          alt="North with the Trade Winds"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full object-cover"
        />

        <!-- Optional supporting copy -->
        <h2
          class="text-neutral-900 font-semibold text-md max-w-3xl leading-tight"
        >
          From our home waters in Singapore to distant shores beyond, we set out
          to build a community bound not by uniform skill or background, but by
          a shared respect for the ocean and an appetite to explore them.
        </h2>

        <img
          src="/images/about/ketam_cleanup.jpg"
          alt="North with the Trade Winds"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full object-cover"
        />

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          Our mission is threefold. First, we champion sustainable seafaring,
          recognising our role as stewards of fragile marine ecosystems. From
          coastal cleanups at Pulau Ketam to workshops on marine life and
          upcycling, we equip our members with the knowledge and practices
          needed to protect the seas for generations to come.
        </p>

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          Second, we aim to build an inclusive community of seafarers, a place
          where beginners can take their first tack alongside seasoned sailors,
          and where curiosity and camaraderie fuel every voyage. Whether it’s a
          leisurely cruise, a regatta, or a weekend dinghy sail, there’s a place
          on deck for everyone.
        </p>

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          Third, we are dedicated to sharing stories and preserving maritime
          heritage. The sea is not only our playground but our library of living
          history. Through oral history projects, digitalising personal
          recounts, photos and videos on our website, we capture the unique
          experiences of each voyage, keeping alive Singapore’s rich seafaring
          traditions and passing them on to future generations.
        </p>

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          Our activities span sailing courses and expeditions, environmental
          initiatives, and cultural preservation projects. From mastering the
          physics of sailing to embarking on long-haul voyages to creating an
          archive of maritime stories that transcends time and borders, we sail
          with purpose.
        </p>

        <img
          src="/images/about/christmas_party_2024.jpg"
          alt="North with the Trade Winds"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-sm w-full object-cover"
        />

        <p class="text-neutral-600 text-md max-w-2xl mt-6">
          At NUS Seafarers, every tack, every cleanup, every tale told brings us
          closer to a single vision: a greener, more connected, and enduring
          maritime culture in Singapore championed by youths, anchored in
          respect for the sea, and driven by the spirit of adventure.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/about/team"
          class="justify-self-start inline-flex items-center px-5 py-3 mt-6 rounded-md text-white bg-neutral-900 hover:bg-neutral-800 transition font-medium text-sm"
        >
          Meet the Team →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
